Error handling in job title and location:
==============================================
if element having xpath //h2[@data-test="search-result-query"] is visible on DOM and also has "Location not found" in it, that is a scenario for wrong/missing location, handle it accordingly.
if element having xpath //*[@id="search-results-heading"] has "No result found" in it, that is a scenario for Job not Found for the value entered in title element, handle it accordingly.

When I enter invalid search criteria
Then I should see an appropriate error message
And no job results should be displayed

Error handling when Backend/API failure (timeout, 500 error)
================================================================

When the search service is unavailable
Then I should see a system error message
And be advised to try again later

================================================================


Error handling when Edges of acceptable input and output
Minimum / maximum number of results

Empty input

Extremely broad input
================================================================
When I search with no preferences selected
Then I should see all available jobs
Sorted by newest Date Posted


When my search returns a large number of jobs
Then the results should be paginated
================================================================

Zero Results Handling
================================================================
When no jobs match my preferences
Then I should see a message indicating no results were found
And I should be able to modify my search criteria
